    <othernotes>Base model by Strawberry Tale&lt;br&gt;Hair and body modifications by Horsecatdraws&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;TARGETS OF INTEREST&lt;br&gt;🐘 Schezo is terrible at catching himself when it comes to his poor phrasing. There's a marker for that.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ But when he's not scuffing his vocab, he plays the straight man to everyone else's antics. That doesn't mean he's devoid of quirks, of course.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ He's one of the more anti-heroic characters from Puyo Puyo's cast. He has honor and morals, but is pretty selfish about his ambitions.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ Tries to keep his cool. Keyword being tries. Default attitude is stoic snark, but calling him a 'creeper' or 'pervert' is the easiest way to piss him off. Getting frisky with his comfort zone can make him lose nerve.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ His knowledge on sexual topics is rather shallow, making the assumption he is a pervert ironic in itself.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ And from the combination of "keep cool until he doesn't" and surface-level sexual knowledge, he can barely handle flirtation.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ Relationship to Arle is pretty complicated.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ Schezo is a dark mage. Doesn't sound like the most friendly title. Additionally, he doesn't look like a typical mage.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ Yes, his sword is translucent. If you ask, he might tell more...&lt;br&gt;⚔️ Magic and other supernatural powers grabs his attention.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ He can be a bit rough around the edges when trying to show his kinder side, but he means what he says. Has a weird way of telling shy and self-deprecating people they're better than they think they are.&lt;br&gt;⚔️ Cute things! He likes cute animal creatures and will (briefly) gush about them.</othernotes>
