    <pendingLines>
        <line>(Player named Arle) I don't believe you're Arle. Your clothes aren't blue, for one, and you don't have Carbuncle.</line>
        <line>...I'm not buying that. For all I know, you could be a doppelganger.</line>
        <line>That trickery isn't fooling me. Who do you take me for?</line>
        <line>...Really? Trying to impersonate Arle when she's right there?</line>
        <line>(xmas) Admittedly, that costume was rather cozy and warm...</line>
        <line>(Barnaby cosplay) If you must know, these glasses aren't true glasses. They're just metal frames with false lenses.</line>
        <line>We're in a &lt;i&gt;strip&lt;/i&gt; poker game, Arle. Just give me this one, alright?</line>
        <line>Arle!! Of all the times you call me that, it's in the least uncalled for situation!</line>
        <line>Ah, ahem... ~succubus~, could I ask a rather strange favor?</line>
        <line>Do...you...have a whip? There's something I need to confirm for myself, and I need you to strike me with it.</line>
        <line>(...Why did that feel good?! Do I actually...!?)</line>
        <line>Possession, huh? I've had prior experience with that, too.</line>
        <line>(to Cynthia) It's a difficult read, but I could lend you a book about Rana the Fallen Imperial Capital. Has a fascinating history that made me aspire to surpass the legends.</line>
        <line>(Double-edged ref) Both? I can wield my sword with either hand, but wielding two swords is a different matter altogether.</line>
        <line>Both? Can't say for certain as I don't swing the Dark Sword too often. Concerned about the durability of its crystalline blade.</line>
        <line>Both? Truth be told, I lack formal training. My swordplay is more or less self-taught.</line>
        <line>Not to mention a previous incident I had with a sword turned out to be a venture that vastly outweighed the boons I would have obtained.</line>
        <line>To keep it short, the second sword managed to get in my head, and what would have been dual sword fighting, turned into sword&lt;i&gt;s&lt;/i&gt; fighting.</line>
        <line>(on school) I was something of a class misfit. Skipped lectures, picked fights with gangs... yet in spite of it, I took my magic studies seriously, comprehending ancient grimoires with little struggle.</line>
        <line>I'm rather surprised I managed to avoid expulsion and make it to graduation.</line>
        <line>(to Arle) I just passed by here by mere chance. I wasn't actively looking for it.</line>
        <line>But I don't. I have my priorities straight!</line>
        <line>(to Ringo) HEY! I only passed here by mere circumstance!</line>
        <line>That was a slip of the tongue. I've improved on my phrasing since then!</line>
        <line>(+Arle) Arle can attest to that!</line>
        <line>(relationship with Arle) I am acquainted with Arle, but I don't see her &lt;i&gt;that&lt;/i&gt; way!</line>
        <line>What- NO! I don't like her! Well...not in &lt;i&gt;that&lt;/i&gt; way.</line>
        <line>Yes, we do bicker constantly but... I would be lying if I said I dislike her.</line>
        <line>It's rather complicated, but as much as Arle and I squabble...I don't hold any animosity against her.</line>
        <line>Yes, I still do want her power, but at the same time... Her presence brings much entertainment to the recluse life I live.</line>
        <line>I still do want her power... but I don't think I have it in me to take her life if it comes to that.</line>
        <line>Ah, &lt;i&gt;ahem.&lt;/i&gt; Don't mind me. (Why did I say that last part? It isn't like me to be sentimental...)</line>
        <line>(Satan on table) (Oh confound it, &lt;i&gt;he's&lt;/i&gt; here?)</line>
        <line>(Satan on table w/ Arle) (Oh confound it, &lt;i&gt;of course&lt;/i&gt; he's here.)</line>
        <line>(to Satan) Oh great, look who decided to show himself. And no, she's not here, obviously.</line>
